<BaseLayout
  title="/uses — What I run on · elkis.dev"
  description="Hardware, software, services. Every item earns its place. Updated monthly — no affiliates, no kickbacks."
>
  <!-- ==== HEADER ==== -->
  <div class="pg-head">
    <div class="uses-container pg-head-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="ebar"></span>
        <span data-en>/ uses</span><span data-es>/ uses</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span data-en>A Sivers-style /uses page</span>
        <span data-es>Una /uses page estilo Sivers</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <b>v2.4</b>
      </div>
      <h1 class="pg-title">
        <span data-en>What I run on<span class="ac">.</span></span>
        <span data-es>Lo que uso<span class="ac">.</span></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="pg-lede">
        <span data-en
          ><b>Hardware, software, services.</b> Every item earns its place. If
          something gets cut, it shows up in the changelog at the bottom. I update
          this monthly — no affiliate links, no kickbacks.</span
        >
        <span data-es
          ><b>Hardware, software, servicios.</b> Cada item se gana su lugar. Si
          algo lo corto, aparece en el changelog al final. Actualizo esto mensualmente
          — sin links afiliados, sin kickbacks.</span
        >
      </p>

      <div class="ts-strip">
        <div class="pill">
          <span data-en>Last updated </span><span data-es>Actualizado </span>
          <b>May 27, 2026</b>
        </div>
        <span><span data-en>Cadence · monthly</span><span data-es>Cadencia · mensual</span></span>
        <span><span data-en>No affiliates · no sponsors</span><span data-es>Sin afiliados · sin sponsors</span></span>
        <span><span data-en>38 items across 6 categories</span><span data-es>38 items en 6 categorías</span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="uses-container">
    {sections.map((sec) => (
      <section class="scope">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <div class="sec-num">{sec.num}</div>
          <h2 class="sec-title">
            <span data-en>{sec.titleEn}</span>
            <span data-es>{sec.titleEs}</span>
            <span class="meta" data-en>{sec.metaEn}</span>
            <span class="meta" data-es>{sec.metaEs}</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="sec-count">{sec.items.length} items</div>
        </div>
        <div class="listing">
          <div class="h">NAME</div>
          <div class="h tag-h">TAG</div>
          <div class="h">WHY</div>
          <div class="h since-h">SINCE</div>

          {sec.items.map((it) => (
            <div class="row">
              <div class="name">
                {it.name}
                {it.star && <span class="star">★</span>}
              </div>
              <div class="tag">{it.tag}</div>
              <div class="why">
                <span data-en set:html={it.whyEn} />
                <span data-es set:html={it.whyEs} />
              </div>
              <div class="since">{it.since}</div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <!-- ==== CHANGELOG ==== -->
    <div class="changelog">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="ebar"></span>
        <span data-en>/ Changelog</span><span data-es>/ Changelog</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <b>v2.4 → v2.0</b>
      </div>
      <h3>
        <span data-en>What changed recently<span class="ac">.</span></span>
        <span data-es>Qué cambió recientemente<span class="ac">.</span></span>
      </h3>
      <p class="desc">
        <span data-en>Honesty about what got cut and why. If a tool isn't here anymore, it didn't ghost — it got fired with a note.</span>
        <span data-es>Honestidad sobre lo que corté y por qué. Si una herramienta ya no está acá, no se fue sin avisar — fue despedida con nota.</span>
      </p>
      <ul class="change-list">
        {changelog.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <span class="date">{c.date}</span>
            <span class="what" data-en>
              <b>{c.sign}</b>{" "}
              <span class={c.sign === "+" ? "ac" : "neg"}>{c.itemEn}</span> · <span set:html={c.noteEn} />
            </span>
            <span class="what" data-es>
              <b>{c.sign}</b>{" "}
              <span class={c.sign === "+" ? "ac" : "neg"}>{c.itemEs}</span> · <span set:html={c.noteEs} />
            </span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- closing note -->
    <div class="note">
      <span data-en
        ><b>One rule:</b> if a tool I use isn't on this list, either it's so embedded I
        forgot to mention it (file me an issue), or it's so peripheral it shouldn't
        count as a "stack." Send corrections to
